From ab9be9284691870b329a39bee70f6b34a52e64d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartheek Palla <palla.kartheekreddy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:42:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] refactor(oid4vc-service): narrow the port to Anand's
 controls

Two changes, both from his conditions on approving this capability.

Removed the per-format credential signing algorithm advertisement that
came across from the older fork branch. It is a real improvement - the
release advertises a Linked-Data suite as an SD-JWT signing algorithm,
which no JOSE wallet can act on - but it is unrelated to
authorization_code, and he said not to carry unrelated changes. The
advertisement is back to exactly what v2.1.0 publishes, and the config
keys that existed only to feed it are gone.

Added the regression coverage he asked for: 'both grants have regression
coverage and do not weaken each other's token, nonce, holder-binding, or
claim-source controls'. Two tests now prove the service still accepts its
own pre-authorised token while Keycloak is enabled, and that the two
sources stay distinguishable - so an offer-bound token cannot be read as
an authenticated subject, or the reverse. Existing coverage only proved
pre-auth with Keycloak switched off.

Writing those tests found the routing detail worth knowing: the service
decides which path to take from the token's UNVERIFIED iss before
verifying anything, so a pre-auth token must be a decodable JWT carrying
the issuer's own URL. My first attempt passed an opaque string and failed
for that reason, not because the behaviour was wrong.

tsc clean; 11 suites / 129 tests pass.
